"THE FIRST ATTEMPT AT THIS CHANGED 227 OF 228 POPULATION READS, and the reason is worth keeping. It flattened with cat, and cat is BINARY -- it appends N(1) to N(2) and ignores the rest, dying on a one-element sequence. Over a two-child cell that is indistinguishable from a flatten, which is exactly the ternary in front of me, so the walk looked right while every longer list lost its tail and every empty one raised. main:flat is the seeded fold that actually flattens. The shape FILE returns was never the problem; the combinator was.",
