"rmap:role_maxpos is the unary check every RMAP-absorbed read and write threads: the greatest role position a fact type uses, DEFAULTING TO 2 when it has none, because the caller asks whether that maximum is 1 and a missing fact type must not answer 'unary'. A default of 0 would invert that test. NOTE the width guard is >= 3, NOT the >= 4 rmap:role_keep carries -- only the fact type and the position are read here, so a three-wide row counts, and engine.py's own comment says so. That is why this is its own restrict rather than rolesof's last pair: reusing rolesof would silently drop rows this must see.",
