"THE GREEDY MACHINE FOLD (the half of machine_fold canon lacked). system:machine folds tau-ordered events with INSERT system:mstep, but readings carry no timestamps: engine.py:3014 machine_fold and its 379-line rust port fire the FIRST FIREABLE event in a fixed order, remove it, and repeat until nothing fires, because a deterministic machine is what makes that greedy walk deterministic. This is that walk, and it needs no new primitive. The state is <status, transitions, todo, held>: an event that cannot fire from the current status moves to held and the scan advances, and a firing transitions the status and resets todo to reverse(held) ++ tl(todo) with held empty, which is what restarts the scan at the front with exactly the fired event consumed. Removal is POSITIONAL, not by value -- the same event type may appear twice and consuming both would skip a transition. It terminates because a firing shrinks the event count and a skip shortens todo, and it stops when todo empties, which is the meaning of nothing fires: events invalid from every reachable status are simply left, the write path no-op semantics machine_fold names. The walk is split so its leftover events are readable: system:mg_run answers the whole final state, system:mgreedy is its status and system:mg_left its unfired events, which is how the caller tells FIRING from MOVING -- a round trip fires without moving, so counting leftovers is the only honest test. mg_left answers them in reverse arrival order, held being built by prepending, so it is a count and an emptiness test, not an order.",

"THE ENTITY SOURCE FOR SM INIT (machine_fold second half). Which keys must materialize the initial status is not bookkeeping, it is an ORM ruling, and engine.py:3014 states it: an entity is an entity by playing a fact. So the source is the noun own rows UNIONED with the role-1 keys of every fact type the noun heads -- a fresh compile carries populations before any table cell materializes, so reading only the noun table would miss entities that plainly exist, and an event that can never fire still evidences its player. The status fact type is excluded from that union by setminus rather than a not-equal filter, since a row already carrying a status is not evidence of a MISSING one. Answers the keys deduped by theta:dedup, which keeps the LAST occurrence -- a b a answers b a -- so this def fixes MEMBERSHIP, not emission order: machine_fold sorts by string before it writes, and the caller is what drops the empty and phi keys and the ones that already carry a status row.",

"THE PER-ENTITY WRITE RULE (machine_fold third piece). Given <current, initial, transitions> and the events for one governed entity, answers <write, status>. The start is the column current status when it has one and the machine initial otherwise. The status is the greedy walk. The WRITE decision is the subtle half and engine.py:3014 states both directions: an entity whose every event is unfireable stays untouched, but a round trip back to where it began still materializes, because the write path would have. So writing is firing AND differing from CURRENT -- not from the start. When there is no current those come apart: a walk that returns to the initial still differs from an absent current and is written, which is exactly SM init landing a status that was missing. Firing is tested by length against system:mg_left rather than by comparing statuses, since a round trip fires without moving.",

