"THE FIRST COMBINING FORM IN CANON. Backus 13.3.2 gives it verbatim -- `Def rhoCONST = 2 o 1; then <CONST,x> in FFP represents the FP functional form x-bar, since, by the metacomposition rule, if y is not bottom, (rho<CONST,x>):y = (rhoCONST):<<CONST,x>,y> = 2o1:<<CONST,x>,y> = x' -- and it has been host code in all eight hosts since the beginning, because the hosts MATCHED the head of a form instead of FETCHING it. That is an FP system, whose forms are `fixed once and for all, and this set determines the power of the system in a major way' (13.1), not an FFP system, where metacomposition `permits the definition of new functional forms, in effect, merely by defining new functions' (13.3.2). The paper calls metacomposition `the only mechanism in the paper', so four certified hosts were certifying a machine the construction does not describe. tau clause (c) went into the js head first, on purpose: java and cs still MATCH the head, so they keep using their own CONST while js resolves this DEF, and byte-identity between them is then a cross-implementation PROOF that the two agree rather than an argument that they should. K(x) is <CONST,x> and canon holds 5737 of them, so this is the hottest form in the system: the host implementations stay as CERTIFIED-EQUAL OVERRIDES (the paper's own escape, and the same shape as render:html -> system:render_html), which is speed, while THIS is the definition of record, which is meaning.",

