"A TENANT IS A CELL WHOSE CONTENTS IS AN ENTIRE STORE (Samuel, 2026-09-11: auto.dev subdomain apps should work together -- PM should be able to assign engineering tasks escalated from support). That is not a design to invent: AREST.tex states it and proves what follows from it. Backus 14.7 gives `a cell in one store may contain another entire store`; the paper's Tenancy paragraph makes a tenant exactly that, so P partitions into per-tenant blocks; and Prop. tenant (Store-relative tenant isolation) proves that for stores in SIBLING tenant cells, no expression formed from the up and down addressing relative to one denotes a cell of the other, because those resolve only cells of their store argument. Visibility follows containment: a parent reaches into its children because their stores are cells in its own, and a child cannot address upward or sideways. Canon had NONE of it -- the word `tenant` appeared once in this file, in a comment about UI panes -- while ast:pop_iscell and ast:pop_sub already recognised and expanded a cell whose contents is a population. So the pieces were here and the surface was not.",
