"TWO EARLIER VERSIONS OF THIS WERE HAND-WRITTEN AND BOTH WERE WRONG. The first listed eighteen canon FUNCTION names and dispatched them by apply; they resolve, but each wanted an operand of its own shape and eight of eight answered operand errors -- the right mechanism against the wrong contract. The second cut to five verbs main dispatches by argv, which works and describes nothing about the model. A table of prose rows is the thing that should not exist here: it is a host verb table that happens to live in canon.",
"AND IT IS state:declared, NOT rmap:fullheads. fullheads answers the fully DERIVED fact types -- 24 of them, marked full in state:derived -- which are exactly the ones a caller CANNOT assert, because rules compute them. state:declared is the model as verbalized: 245 fact types, every one carrying its player types, so a tool and its signature are one row. Reading the wrong registry served the wrong 24 with empty signatures, and made the roles look missing when they were one cell away.",
