"AND A NAME THE ROUTER SENDS ELSEWHERE IS NOT A TOOL FOR IT (2026-09-11). main:api tests ui:groups BEFORE main:declared_names, so a name that is both an entity table and a fact type -- an OBJECTIFIED fact type, which is both by construction -- is routed to the collection arm whatever the tool list says. support carries two: `Customer pursues Use Case` objectified as Integration, `Plan includes API` as PlanProduct. Each was offered as a fact-type tool advertising its two role players, and POSTing them answered 201 committed with the population still at 0 rows -- the first player was read as the entity id and the second as a fact type with no value, so the collection arm minted an id and asserted nothing. A door that reports success and writes nothing is the wrong-answer shape, so the tool list now drops what the router will not treat as a fact type, and mcp:entities offers the same name with the schema the route actually takes. WHAT THIS DOES NOT FIX, and it is why the two are named here: rmap gives an objectified fact type's OWN roles no column -- PlanProduct's table is <k, PlanProductHasPricePerCall> and `Plan includes API` is in no table at all -- so there is still no door that asserts one. There was none before either; there was a door that said there was.",
