"AN ALETHIC c REJECTS THE COMMIT, A DEONTIC c WARNS AND COMMITS -- AREST.tex:189 in one sentence, and Thm 1 is written on it: D-prime carries P-double-prime iff V has no ALETHIC violation, a condition that says nothing unless deontic violations are IN V. This answered two outcomes for a three-outcome vocabulary: http:status has declared committed_with_violations -> 200 all along, beside committed -> 201 and refused -> 409, and nothing could ever produce the middle one. NOTHING NEW IS BUILT HERE. A violation already carries its constraint FAMILY in slot 2 -- <ftid, uniqueness, binding> -- and ConstraintTypeHasConstraintTypeFamily already holds 24 rows whose families are ring, uniqueness, mandatory, frequency, value, set-comparison, subset, equality, cardinality and DEONTIC (DF_pop, DF_cwa, DF_owa, DO_pop, DO_obl, DO_sender). So the modality of a violation is the family it is tagged with, the data was in the store the whole time, and the only thing missing was the branch that reads it.",
